// Title: Rebuild Performance Counter Values Via Lodctr.EXE
// Sigma ID: cc9d3712-6310-4320-b2df-7cb408274d53
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-06-15 | Modified: 2024-03-05
// ATT&CK: execution
// Description: Detects the execution of "lodctr.exe" to rebuild the performance counter registry values. This
//   can be abused by attackers by providing a malicious config file to overwrite performance counter
//   configuration to confuse and evade monitoring and security solutions.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate usage by an administrator
// References:
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/security/identity-protection/virtual-smart-cards/virtual-smart-card-tpmvscmgr
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_lodctr_performance_counter_tampering.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\lodctr.exe" and ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "LODCTR.EXE") and (ProcessCommandLine contains " -r" or ProcessCommandLine contains " /r" or ProcessCommandLine contains " –r" or ProcessCommandLine contains " —r" or ProcessCommandLine contains " ―r")
